<title>UK: National Grid up on reports of job cuts.</title>
<headline>National Grid up on reports of job cuts.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in National Grid were indicated higher in pre-market dealings on Monday following weekend press reports that the electricity transmission concern will cut 750 jobs in an effort to save one billion stg over four years, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 0181 GMT, the shares were up 2p to 196-1/2p, the highest price since mid-May.  </p>
<p>National Grid is set to release its interim profits on Tuesday. Half year profits are seen up to 279 million to 304 million stg from 278.9 million a year ago.</p>
<p>But the market is expected to focus equally on indications on how the company will cope with new pricing controls, which go into effect on April 1, 1997, analysts said.</p>
<p>--Debra Sherman, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
